---
// The pre-paint assignment: the theme.
//
// Upstream's ThemeProvider ships two things: this script, and a
// `<template id="theme-icons">` holding three `<svg>` icons for
// `<starlight-theme-select>`. This site replaced that dropdown with
// ThemeToggle, which draws its own icons — so the template fed a picker no page
// contains, and the closure's `updatePickers()` walked a `querySelectorAll`
// that never matched. Both shipped on every page anyway.
//
// The assignment stays. It has to run before first paint or the page flashes
// the wrong theme, and its exact behaviour is a contract src/lib/theme.ts is
// written against: an empty stored value means auto, and any stored value that
// is not 'light' means dark.
//
// The storage check sits inside the try: a browser that blocks site data throws
// on the first touch of `localStorage`, `typeof` included, and a throw here
// would leave the theme unset until after first paint.
//
// A reader's choice from the HTML pages carries over. They stored it under
// `kb-theme` (the HTML site's theme script), `light` or `dark`, nothing for auto; with
// no Starlight value yet, that one is read and copied across once, so the
// first visit here opens in the theme the reader picked there.
//
// It stays `is:inline` because that is what EXTERNALIZABLE_SCRIPTS in
// tools/src/site/site-portable.ts recognises and rewrites to
// `_astro/sl-theme.<hash>.js` — a classic external script runs synchronously at
// the same position on both protocols, so the pre-paint guarantee survives the
// move and the body is not spelled into every page. Change a byte of it and
// that fingerprint changes with it, or the script silently stays inline and
// check-site-absence reports it.
//
// `window.StarlightThemeProvider` is gone. Its only caller in the whole of
// Starlight is `components/ThemeSelect.astro`, which `components:` in
// astro.config.mjs points at ThemeToggle instead.
---

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    const storedTheme = (() => {
      try {
        if (typeof localStorage === 'undefined') return null;
        const own = localStorage.getItem('starlight-theme');
        if (own !== null) return own;
        const carried = localStorage.getItem('kb-theme');
        if (carried !== 'light' && carried !== 'dark') return null;
        localStorage.setItem('starlight-theme', carried);
        return carried;
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
    })();
    const theme =
      storedTheme ||
      (window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark');
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme === 'light' ? 'light' : 'dark';
  })();
</script>
